1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:08,354
(Q31) We've been discussing the factors the architect has to consider when designing domestic buildings.

2
00:00:08,354 --> 00:00:13,360
I'm going to move on now to consider the design of public buildings,

3
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:21,869
and I'll illustrate this by referring to the new Taylor Concert Hall that's recently been completed here in the city.

4
00:00:21,869 --> 00:00:31,506
So, as with a domestic building, when designing a public building, an architect needs to consider the function of the building

5
00:00:31,506 --> 00:00:40,275
for example, is it to be used primarily for entertainment, or for education, or for administration?

6
00:00:40,275 --> 00:00:46,439
The second thing the architect needs to think about is the context of the building,

7
00:00:46,439 --> 00:00:54,044
[Q31答案句【social】， 连接词] this includes its physical location, obviously, but it also includes the social meaning of the building,

8
00:00:54,044 --> 00:00:57,016
how it relates to the people it's built for.

9
00:00:57,016 --> 00:01:07,441
(Q32) And finally, for an important public buildings, the architect may also be looking for a centralsymbolic idea on which to base the design,

10
00:01:07,441 --> 00:01:12,925
a sort of metaphor for the building and the way in which it is used.

11
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:17,966
Let's look at the new Taylor Concert Hall in relation to these ideas.

12
00:01:17,966 --> 00:01:25,368
[Q32跟定位词 site] The location chosen was a site in a run-down district that has been ignored in previous redevelopment plans.

13
00:01:25,368 --> 00:01:30,229
[Q32答案句【factory】] It was occupied by a factory that had been empty for some years.

14
00:01:30,229 --> 00:01:38,111
(Q33) The whole area was some distance from the high-rise office blocks of the central business district and shopping centre,

15
00:01:38,111 --> 00:01:41,279
but it was only one kilometre from the ring road.

16
00:01:41,279 --> 00:01:52,153
[Q33答案句【canal】， be bordered to = besides 在...旁边] The site itself was bordered to the north by a canal which had once been used by boats bringing in raw materials when the area was used for manufacturing.

17
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:56,744
(Q34) The architect chosen for the project was Tom Harrison.

18
00:01:56,744 --> 00:02:05,090
He found the main design challenge was the location of the site in an area that had no neighbouring buildings of any importance.

19
00:02:05,090 --> 00:02:13,238
To reflect the fact that the significance of the building in this quite run-down location was as yet unknown,

20
00:02:13,238 --> 00:02:22,589
[Q34跟定位： mystery] he decided to create a building centred around the idea of a mystery - something whose meaning still has to be discovered.

21
00:02:22,589 --> 00:02:27,433
[Q34小标题跟定位] So how was this reflected in the design of the building?

22
00:02:27,433 --> 00:02:36,336
Well, Harrison decided to create pedestrian access to the building and to make use of the presence of water on the site.&nbsp;

23
00:02:36,336 --> 00:02:42,090
[Q34答案句【bridge】，代词指代的升级版， pedestrian access, access指的指什么要继续听， 听到approach，确定是 bridge这个词] As people approach the entrance, they therefore have to cross over a bridge.

24
00:02:42,090 --> 00:02:49,657
(Q35) He wanted to give people a feeling of suspense as they see the building first from a distance, and then close-up,

25
00:02:49,657 --> 00:02:56,460
[Q35答案句【box】， shape of 原词，跟后面的词 was that of a BOX] and the initial impression he wanted to create from the shape of the building as a whole was that of a box.

26
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:04,743
(Q36) The first side that people see, the southern wall, is just a high, flat wall uninterrupted by any windows.

27
00:03:04,743 --> 00:03:10,388
This might sound off-putting, but it supports Harrison's concept of the building

28
00:03:10,388 --> 00:03:15,552
that the person approaching is intrigued and wonders what will be inside.

29
00:03:15,552 --> 00:03:19,515
And this flat wall also has another purpose.

30
00:03:19,515 --> 00:03:31,742
[Q36答案句【screen】 huge=large] At night-time, projectors are switched on and it functions as a huge screen, onto which images are projected.

31
00:03:31,742 --> 00:03:35,862
(Q37) The auditorium itself seats 1500 people.

32
00:03:35,862 --> 00:03:39,771
The floor's supported by ten massive pads.

33
00:03:39,771 --> 00:03:48,643
[Q37答案句【rubber】， be constructed from = be made of] These are constructed from rubber, and so are able to absorb any vibrations from outside and prevent them from affecting the auditorium.

34
00:03:48,643 --> 00:03:55,685
(Q38) The walls are made of several layers of honey-coloured wood, all sourced from local beech trees.

35
00:03:55,685 --> 00:04:04,697
[Q38答案句【curved】,听否定词 not straight  they are curved] In order to improve the acoustic properties of the auditorium and to amplify the sound, they are not straight, they are curved.

36
00:04:04,697 --> 00:04:11,796
(Q39) The acoustics are also adjustable according to the size of orchestra and the type of music being played.

37
00:04:11,796 --> 00:04:27,899
[Q39答案句【curtains】] In order to achieve this, there are nine movable panels in the ceiling above the orchestra which are all individually motorized,and the walls also have curtains which can be opened or closed to change the acoustics.

38
00:04:27,899 --> 00:04:32,817
(Q40) The reaction of the public to the new building has generally been positive.

39
00:04:32,817 --> 00:04:38,208
However, the evaluation of some critics has been less enthusiastic.

40
00:04:38,208 --> 00:04:48,065
[Q40答案句【 international】] In spite of Harrison s efforts to use local materials, they criticise the style of the design as being international rather than local,

41
00:04:48,065 --> 00:04:50,565
and say it doesn't reflect features of the landscape or society for which it is built.

